  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nThe forecast is very straight-forward through the next week, and\nconfidence is therfore high in the forecast details. Global model\nensembles agree that an anomalously warm upper level ridge will \nslowly shift eastward across the lower Mississippi Valley region\nas we finish up the week and go into next week. This will lead to\na continuation of dry weather with large diurnal temperature \nranges appoaching 40 deg F. Of greatest importance, the continued\ndrying of vegetation combined with exceptionally low daytime RH\nvalues will help to maintain an elevated fire danger threat. We \nwill continue to message this through the graphics and fire danger\nstatement. Wind should have less influence and be a smaller \nfactor in determining the fire danger threat levels. Otherwise, \nrainfall is not expected until late next week at the earliest, \nwhen the ridge shows signs of breaking down. /EC/",
